Taxonomy and Layer 2 Configuration
This section outlines the domain-specific taxonomy used for the crop insurance purchase use case and defines the expected configurations.
Domain
Domain Code
financial-services:uki
Purpose
Enables discovery, purchase, and fulfillment of micro-insurance products for farmers, with digitally verifiable policies, policy documents, nominee assignments, and payout tracking.
crop-insurance
Insurance products that provide coverage against natural risks (e.g., rainfall irregularity, drought, pest) for a specific crop and time duration.


Fulfillment Types
Code
Description
Digital
The policy is issued digitally. Documents are sent via link or email/SMS post confirmation.


Provider Tags
Code
Description
agent-rating
Rating of the BPP / issuing provider
claim-settlement-ratio
Historical ratio of claims settled by the provider
verified-provider
Whether provider is certified by the insurance regulator
years-of-operation
Number of years provider has operated


Item Tags
Code
Description
premium
Cost of the policy (base premium per unit/acre)
sum-insured
Coverage offered in ₹ (per acre)
duration
Number of days/weeks/months covered
coverage
Description of what is covered (e.g., rainfall deviation)
refund-policy
Whether refund is allowed post-confirmation
payout-matrix
How payouts are computed (e.g., IMD-linked)
nominee
One or more assigned beneficiaries
aadhaar-required
Whether Aadhaar is mandatory for KYC
ownership-status
Whether farmer self-declares ownership
kyc-documents
Optional or required documents (Aadhaar, land ownership)


Quote Rules
Field
Value
TTL for Quote
PT10M
TTL for Init
PT5M
Currency
INR
Payment Type
PRE-FULFILLMENT
Payment Collected By
BPP
Default Refund Policy
Non-refundable post issuance
Documents Format
PDF, downloadable via HTTPS URL


Document Handling
Rule
Description
Policy docs must be hosted by BPP
URL must be permanent or backed by retention SLA
Must be in .pdf format
Minimum metadata: name, date, validity period, transaction/order ID
Document links
Shared under order.documents[]



